From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:55:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: Allow the AdaptiveFirFilter SIMD suite to be empty

All tests in AdaptiveFirFilterOneTwoFourEightRenderChannels are for x86 or
NEON optimizations, so on other targets (or ARM without NEON) the suite is
instantiated without any tests, which gtest reports as a failure.
---
diff --git a/webrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/adaptive_fir_filter_unittest.cc b/webrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/adaptive_fir_filter_unittest.cc
--- a/webrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/adaptive_fir_filter_unittest.cc
+++ b/webrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/adaptive_fir_filter_unittest.cc
@@ -70,6 +70,9 @@
 INSTANTIATE_TEST_SUITE_P(MultiChannel,
                          AdaptiveFirFilterOneTwoFourEightRenderChannels,
                          ::testing::Values(1, 2, 4, 8));
+// All tests in this suite are for SIMD optimizations, so there may be none.
+GTEST_ALLOW_UNINSTANTIATED_PARAMETERIZED_TEST(
+    AdaptiveFirFilterOneTwoFourEightRenderChannels);
 
 #if defined(WEBRTC_HAS_NEON)
 // Verifies that the optimized methods for filter adaptation are similar to
-- 
2.49.0

